  "id": "d1dc9dbd-cb7d-5b6a-9c5f-2f9619b8db00",
  "slug": "peanut-butter-banana-muffins-recipe-8642312",
  "name": "Peanut Butter Banana Muffins",
  "recipe_type": "breakfast",
  "brief_description": "Chef John\u2019s peanut butter banana muffins bring chocolate into the famous mix of peanut butter and bananas, with a piped peanut butter icing to make them even prettier. In both taste and texture, this is an absolutely beautiful muffin.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Line a 12-cup muffin tin with paper liners, or grease cups. Whisk together flour, salt, baking powder, and baking soda; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Beat butter, peanut butter, and sugar together in a bowl with an electric mixer or whisk until light and fluffy. Add bananas and beat again until light and fluffy. Mix in eggs one at a time; stir in milk and vanilla."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Add flour mixture; mix on low speed until about 75% of flour is incorporated. Use a spatula to stir in chocolate chips, and to fully incorporate flour. Divide batter evenly between prepared muffin cups."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a toothpick inserted near the center comes out clean, 23 to 25 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Cool muffins in the tin for about 15 minutes; transfer to a wire rack to cool completely, about 15 minutes more."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "For icing, combine peanut butter, milk, and powdered sugar in a bowl and stir until a thick icing is formed. Add more powdered sugar as needed for an icing thick enough to hold its shape when piped. Add icing to a piping bag and pipe in a zigzag pattern over cooled muffins."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 25,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
